## Files excluded intentionally

`Inventory/exclusions.jsonl` lists exact paths or subtrees and the reason for excluding them. Exclusions include credential stores, private signing material, browser or device authentication state, runtime and package caches, vendored dependency installations, and unpacked vendor installations. The standalone 406,944,100-byte official Blender 5.3.0 Linux installer is included for offline setup. Its SHA-256 matched Blender’s official release manifest. The repository’s lockfiles, Gradle wrapper, dependency metadata, setup notes, Blender authoring scripts, editable scenes and pinned-tool source records are preserved. Third-party documentation or bundled package entries that resembled embedded credentials were conservatively excluded from local tool snapshots. Filename and content checks covered source, text records and readable nested ZIPs. Never put a service credential into the shareable backup.

Machine-specific SDK paths and private service secrets should be established on the restored workstation. `services.env.example` contains placeholders. Dependencies and disposable development caches are reproducible from the lockfiles and tool records. Original workspace symlinks are indexed. A symlink targeting a discarded tool cache or an absent machine path requires reinstallation or reconnection.

